          %h2#references References
          %p
            Stasheff implicitly described the operad of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associahedra"} associahedra
            in
          %ul
            %li#Stasheff63a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Dillon+Stasheff"}> James Dillon Stasheff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopy associativity of H-spaces I
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1993608"} web
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Dillon+Stasheff"}> James Dillon Stasheff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopy associativity of H-spaces II
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1993609"} web
          %p but without making the abstract concept of operad explicit. The abstract definition (as well as the name) is originally due to
          %ul
            %li#May1972
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
              ,
              %em The geometry of iterated loop spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/gils.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            An earlier version was the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analyser"} analyser
            (known usually by French version
            = succeed ")," do
              %em analyseur
          %ul
            %li
              M. Lazard,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lois de groupes et analyseurs
              %strong 72
              (1955), pp. 299–400.
          %p Monographs:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Kriz"}> Igor Kriz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Operads, algebras, modules and motives
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 233
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/PAPERS/kmbooklatex.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=AST_1995__233__1_0"} numdam:AST_1995__233__1_0
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Leinster"}> Tom Leinster
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher operads, higher categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 298
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.CT/0305049"} math.CT/0305049
            %li#MarklShniderStasheff
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Markl"}> Martin Markl
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Shnider"} Steve Shnider
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} James D. Stasheff
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Operads in algebra, topology and physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 96
            %li#Markl2008
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Markl"}> Martin Markl
                , Operads and PROPS, In volume 5 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Handbook of Algebra
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0601129"} arXiv:math/0601129
            %li
              %p
                V.A. Smirnov,
                %em Simplicial and operad methods in algebraic topology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Loday"}> Jean-Louis Loday
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruno+Vallette"} Bruno Vallette
                = succeed ":" do
                  %em Algebraic operads
                %strong 346
                Springer (2012) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9783642303616"}> ISBN 978-3-642-30362-3
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-30362-3"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-30362-3
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.univ-paris13.fr/~vallette/Operads.pdf"} pdf
            %li#FresseMOF
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benoit+Fresse"}> Benoit Fresse
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Modules over operads and functors
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 1967
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2494775"} MR2010e:18009
            %li#FresseHOGTG
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benoit+Fresse"}> Benoit Fresse
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopy of Operads and Grothendieck-Teichmüller Groups (Volumes 1 &amp; 2)
                %strong 217
                (2017) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-217/"}> ISBN:978-1-4704-3480-9
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.univ-lille1.fr/~fresse/OperadHomotopyBook/"} website
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.648.9110&rep=rep1&type=pdf"} pdf (draft of Part I)
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+Trimble"}> Todd Trimble
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/toddtrimble/published/Notes+on+operads+and+the+Lie+operad"} Notes on operads and the Lie operad
              (
              %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/trimble/trimble_lie_operad.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rectification"} rectification
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+operad"} symmetric
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colored+operads"} colored operads
          %ul
            %li#PavlovScholbach18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Pavlov"}> Dmitri Pavlov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jakob+Scholbach"} Jakob Scholbach
              = succeed "," do
                %em Admissibility and rectification of colored symmetric operads
              %strong 11
              3 (2018) 559-601
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/topo.12008"} doi:10.1112/topo.12008
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1410.5675"} arXiv:1410.5675
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p
            Hermida constructed a monadic 2-adjunction between the 2-category of nonsymmetric colored operads in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Set
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Set, \times)
            (which he calls
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multicategories"} multicategories
          %ul
            %li#Hermida2000
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Hermida"}> Claudio Hermida
              , Representable multicategories, Advances in Mathematics, Volume 151, Issue 2, 2000, 164-225. (
              %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0001870899918777/"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Elmendorf and Mandell constructed an adjunction between the category of symmetric colored operads in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Set
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Set, \times)
            (which they call “multicategories”) and the category of symmetric strict monoidal categories (which they call “permutative categories”) in Theorem 4.3 of this paper:
          %ul
            %li#ElmendorfMandell2007
              A. D. Elmendorf and M. A. Mandell,
              %em Permutative categories, multicategories, and algebraic K-theory
              Algebraic &amp; Geometric Topology 9.4 (2009): 2391-2441. (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0710.0082"}> arXiv:0710.0082
              )
          %p
            Weber treated a related adjunction at the 2-categorical level in Section 3.3 of this paper, using the term “symmetric multicategory” to mean the same thing as “colored operad in
            = succeed "\u201D:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Set, \times)
          %ul
            %li#Weber2009
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Weber"}> Mark Weber
              , Free products of higher operad algebras. (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0909.4722"}> arXiv:0909.4722
              )
          %p
            On operads as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+functors"} double functors
            between certain
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+categories"} double categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Pisani"}> Claudio Pisani
              ,
              %em Operads as double functors
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.07028"}> arXiv:2208.07028
              )
